00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.400 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to the new world  review your source for everything anime  and manga today I'm just here to talk a  little bit about a series that I am  particularly excited for in the upcoming  summer season which is dr. Stern and it  officially begins airing on the 5th of  July so is still a while away if you  have not already heard of this property  I would like to put it on your radar now  and I'll start by giving the synopsis  which goes a little something like this  one fateful day all the humanity was  petrified  by a blinding flash of light after  several millennia high school but I'd  you awakens and finds himself lost in a  world of statues however he's not alone  his science loving friend sank who's  been up and running for a few months and  he's got a grand plan in mind to  kick-start civilization with the power  of science so I've been reading dr.  Stein for quite some time now and seeing  the previews for the anime adaptation  here have me pretty pumped now what I'll  say from the outset is that this series  is pretty much just pure fun it doesn't  have too many overly serious plot  elements to it in fact if you're  familiar with shokugeki no souma or food  wars which ever you prefer to say then  I'd very much equate it to that except  instead of cooking we're focusing on  science in general but honestly I don't  think that comparison quite does dr.  stone justice because when you take a  step back from it you realize that its  scope is just so massive as its  characters are charged with the mission  of restoring an entire human history's  worth of technological advances and they  have to do so from a literal Stone Edge  so I guess what I'm trying to say is  that it has a feeling of progress that  food was is very much lacking you know  every innovation opens up a door for 10  other future innovations and at certain  points in the series you look back on  the beginning and just go  we've been on an incredible journey and  some of the things that they make in the  series are guaranteed to blow your mind  on a regular basis which really is the  wonder of science I guess now during my  schooling period I was one of those kids  who didn't really pay much attention  during any for science except for  biology although admittedly only because  my teacher was she was pretty hard so I  wasn't sure how much interest I'd have  in doctor stone before picking it up and  if any of you are in a similar position  let me just tell you that this series  showcases science in such a brilliant  and fanciful manner it's still  maintaining a very solid grounding and  even makes things as simple as possible  for the reader to understand whilst not  talking down to them and that's a  problem I thought I would initially have  with its protagonists ank-ooo he is the  scientific genius / time capsule that  makes the entire series work and reading  the first couple of chapters I was very  afraid that he was going to be kind of  like your standard arrogant genius stick  but despite his frankly absurd  intelligence the series does an Incred  job of making him relatable approachable  and very easy to root for and  interestingly in the anime adaptation  he's going to be voiced by yusuke  kobayashi  is probably best known for performing  subaru from re0 and i associate his  voice very strongly with that character  so it's going to be really interesting  to hear him play such a radically  different role in speaking of radically  different roles doctor Stern also  features a pretty incredible supporting  cast all of whom have their own  particular skills a greatly assists the  mission of restoring science to the  staring world many of whom aren't even  featured in the trailers but once again  I'll draw the food Wiles comparison by  stating that it really is an ensemble  series and the auxilary characters are a  major part of what makes it so much fun  to read and I'm sure to watch as well  although if I had one negative that  should probably be flagged before  watching it's that many of the  characters in my opinion can be a bit  ropey like each of them will have strong  core ideas or beliefs but if you're  looking for anything with a bit more  depth or subtlety you won't find that  and dr. stein because after spending  about a minute with each character  you'll know what they're about instantly  and with a few notable exceptions they  they won't be changing I'd also argue  that it isn't necessarily a bad thing  though because these trophy and  archetypal characters do really allow  the core theme of the show to shine by  acting as a simplistic juxtaposition  some of the science can already be  complicated enough as it is so I think  having simple characters really helps in  regards to inviting the audience into a  topic that by and large would generally  poor and confuse them not only that but  their energy makes whatever science  they're exploring at the time just so  much fun to learn about and even though  I've probably retained a minuscule  amount of what has actually been taught  in the series it does at least give you  the illusion of feeling smarter  afterwards now if anything I'd say that  dr. stone is going to be an even more  incredible experience to watch because  as much as I love the manga there are  periods of huge science the exposition  that I think will really benefit from an  animated medium it's a moving diagrams  and a wonderful vocal performance to go  along with them now with all of this in  mind the only way I think the show could  really fail is if it is handed over to a  poor production company and dr. stone  has been put in the hands of TMS  entertainment and if you're not familiar  with them they are one of the oldest  anime studios in existence having  produced some incredible classics such  as Akira and Lupin the third but moving  into the more modern era they do have  some experience in long-running Shonen  having produced d.gray-man which is  pretty great for its time and even more  recently megalo box so I'm not  particularly worried about dr. stone  from an animation perspective at all and  everything we've seen in the preview so  far look wonderfully schmack and now I  suppose I should be careful not to over  rate the series too much and if you  spend any amount of time looking up  towards CERN on the Internet at all you  probably come across a lot of talk about  the potential  dr. stone to become one of the new-age  big three I mean if such a thing really  exists anymore it's more like the big  one now now I love this series but I  really don't quite know about that it's  a pretty big call to make but I might  not be able to see it that way because  of how unconventional dr. stone is for a  shounen series I mean the undisputed  champions of Shonen have always been  battle manga and that is not dr. stein  if you're looking for an action focus  series this isn't really going to do it  for you so I don't know if that is put a  glass ceiling on dr. stone but it does  still have potential I also have to  acknowledge that we're barely over 100  chapters into it and thinking back on  where world-changing series like one  piece were at 100 chapters in I probably  wouldn't have gone so far as to label it  a future member of the big three either  I mean it was a fantastic story no but  one piece had an awfully long way to go  to reach his full potential and it's  arguably still on its journey over two  decades in and that could be dr. Stein  you know when you're trying to condense  more or less the entirety of human  technological innovation into a singular  experience you've got a lot to play with  in a near infinite amount of directions  that the series could be taken and I  mean who's to say that it would simply  stop when or if humanity is restored why  not keep pushing science beyond what we  know and getting into some true  innovation and yes I know I'm probably  going in a wild tangent here so let's  wrap this up before I go too much  further but my overall point is that I  think the series very much deserves your  attention it's fun  fresh and I highly recommend you all  check it out when it begins airing on  the fifth of July but that pretty much  does it for this short rambling  discussion thing on why I think you  should watch dr. stone if you enjoyed  this video when the content this channel  produced in general and please do  consider donating to the New World  review patreon because the support of  all of your amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share or subscribe because it also helps  plot this channel an incredible amount  if you'd like to join the fun at any  time then please do head over to my  discord server where a wide array of  shenanigan retakes place on a daily  basis and finally please do comment with  your thoughts on dr. Stein this has been  the New World review and I'll see you  next time  you  [Music]

